# What a published extension does not need.
#
# vsce packages everything not listed here, which by default meant shipping the
# TypeScript source, the build config, the integration tests and a 602KB source
# map — around two thirds of the download, none of it reachable at runtime. The
# bundle in dist/ is what actually runs.

# Source and build inputs; dist/extension.js is the built artifact.
src/**
tsconfig.json
.vscodeignore

# Tests. They run in CI against a real VS Code, not on a user's machine.
test/**

# A source map nobody can act on: the bundle is generated, and the sources it
# points at are not shipped.
dist/**/*.map

# Editor and tooling noise.
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
